# Primary Directives

## Project Focus

This is a **DSA (Data Structures and Algorithms) learning repository** that:
- Provides structured modules from complexity analysis to hashing and problem patterns
- Emphasizes original implementations, complexity analysis, and clean Python 3.12+ code
- Supports interview preparation and problem-solving methodology
- Enforces a zero-copy policy (no verbatim copy from solution sites)

## Current State

- ✅ Project planning and documentation complete (README, CONTRIBUTING)
- ✅ Repository structure and CI (pytest, black, isort, flake8) established
- ⏳ Module content (01_… through 07_…) – In progress
- ⏳ Test coverage and practice sets – In progress

## Documentation Accuracy

- README and docs must match actual layout and behaviour
- Module structure and file naming must follow CONTRIBUTING and README
- No misleading technology or project descriptions

## Code Maintenance

- Follow PEP 8; use type hints and docstrings
- Include time/space complexity comments for solutions
- Place code in correct module folders and tests in `tests/`
- Enforce zero-copy policy; keep content original and transformative
